    "reason": "Only 47.2% of residual DEK leaks are on duplicated prompts (<50%). Leak rate dup vs unique: image_swap 20.0% vs 20.0%; hard_negative 65.0% vs 43.3%.",
    "plan_threshold_text_gate": 0.7,
    "foreign_same_prompt_share": 0.4098360655737705,
    "mechanism_note": "Plan thresholds: >=70%% of residual leak locations on duplicated query prompts => text gate; we observe 47.2%% (below 50%% => do not build residual story on duplication). Separate mechanism check: among DEK foreign fires, the retrieved expert shares the query prompt in 25%% of image_swap foreign (3/12) and 45%% of hard_negative foreign (22/49); overall 41%%. Hard-negative is the only place with a partial same-prompt signal; image-swap residual foreign is mostly different-prompt (vision/other). Verdict: unexplained / not text-gate-dominated; move on. Dataset-level VLKEB vs EVQA gap still correlates with dup rate (40%% vs 2.7%%).",
    "paper_guidance": "One short paragraph: VLKEB residual tracks dataset prompt duplication at a coarse level, but residual foreign experts are usually not prompt siblings; do not claim text-gate failure as the residual mechanism. Optional G2: text margin / top-K text set size ablation without making it the paper center."
